  "preparation_failures": [
    "Initial257-byte fragmented PUBLISH could be fully locally accepted before the coordinator closed it. Initial Windows shared matrix failed the strict partial precondition; a delayed diagnostic demonstrated accepted=291 wire=291. Seven completed initial matrices are retained but not used as final acceptance. The strict assertion is preserved.",
    "Initial16KiB/64KiB TCP output settings were smaller than the TLS context send budget; typed setup rejection was correct and archived. Matched64KiB context/native queues plus512KiB payload are used finally.",
    "An intermediate1MiB payload plus MQTT headers exceeded the default1MiB full-packet limit and stalled the wire-cut barrier. Source inspection led to512KiB payload. Its mutable prototype report/log was overwritten by the corrected72-case prototype; this failure is disclosed, not counted as passing or claimed fully archived.",
    "After enlarging the payload, tiny peer receive windows on both connections caused WSL static/ASan replay barrier timeouts; both failed rows and successful resource reaping are retained. The tiny window is now first-connection-only; all eight final matrices rerun with the corrected proxy.",
    "A prior shell-quoting preparation failure in the ordinary Windows broker launch was fixed before the actual cases; its log is retained. No failed stage is counted as final success."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "TLS authenticates native client to bounded Python/OpenSSL; independent Mosquitto2.1.2 backend is local TCP, not native broker TLS",
    "Custom asynchronous Resolver, not system DNS; no enhanced-auth broker plugin or corrupted TLS record injection",
    "Volatile explicit reconnect only; no broker restart/durable/automatic recovery or WebSocket qualification",
    "Functional runs may overlap; no performance measurement or new performance claim. Existing throughput/tail-latency failures and noise limits stay open",
    "Windows native and WSL Linux evidence only; native Linux deployment,>=72h and complete four-product production acceptance remain open"
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Assigned client ids, automatic/durable recovery and WebSocket",
    "Other broker and enhanced-auth plugin interoperability",
